TIGHT-TOLERANCE REPEAT of a few cases (reltol 1e-6, vntol 1e-9 for the DC operating point AND the transient; abstol stays 1e-12: with 1e-15 every run aborts at the first switching event,
  "Timestep too small ... vck#branch", the abort class of Decision 43a): the settling numbers without the DC-solve difference of the two copies (see the NOTE in lp_rvt_settle.log).
STAGE settle (D5 item 1 method, AFE/adc/scripts/d5lib.py + d5_settle.py, their netlist builder and case list): TWO copies of the amplifier in one netlist, L loaded by the REAL sampling TG +
  split 6+6 DAC + cmp_p (AFE/adc/spice), U unloaded (20 fF); frame 0 at 2 ms leaves the bottoms at the previous code, the TG closes after T_CONV 9.5 us (the kick), acquisition 240.5 us;
  error = out_L - out_U at the next CS falling [LSB].  Case = <level>_<previous level>_<kick polarity p / m / 0>.  Differences to D5: .options abstol=1e-12 (D5 had 1e-15, the abort cause),
  one ngspice thread.  D5 result (sim/d5_settle.log, 57 runs): <= 0.086 / 0.114 / 0.070 LSB (typ / ff 85 / ss -40), spikes up to 362 LSB.
