SUMMARY per variant and corner (4 cases each) [LSB = 0.806 mV]: END = max |L-U| at the end of T_ACQ (the D5 number); CHANGE = max |(L-U at the end) - (L-U before the frame)| = what the
  kick leaves; STATIC = L-U before the frame (range over the cases); SPIKE = largest |L-U| in the 5 us after the TG closes
  orig           typ: 4 runs, END 0.086, CHANGE 0.090, STATIC -0.006..-0.002, SPIKE 288 LSB = 232 mV | ff85: 4 runs, END 0.094, CHANGE 0.089, STATIC -0.001..+0.005, SPIKE 303 LSB = 244 mV | ss-40: 4 runs, END 0.064, CHANGE 0.075, STATIC -0.019..-0.002, SPIKE 272 LSB = 219 mV
  rvt            typ: 4 runs, END 0.023, CHANGE 0.022, STATIC -0.001..+0.001, SPIKE 219 LSB = 176 mV | ff85: 4 runs, END 0.011, CHANGE 0.010, STATIC -0.000..+0.000, SPIKE 233 LSB = 188 mV | ss-40: 4 runs, END 0.026, CHANGE 0.026, STATIC -0.007..+0.008, SPIKE 203 LSB = 164 mV

NOTE on STATIC (L-U before any ADC event): it is the difference of the two copies in the DC operating point of the run.  The output DC level is out = vn2 + (leakage at the summing node) x R(pseudo-R),
  i.e. it is set by currents of 1e-17 A in 5 TOhm, and the DC solution of such a node is only as good as the Newton stop criterion (reltol 1e-4 x 1.65 V = 165 uV = 0.2 LSB): the two copies
  can stop up to that far apart, and the transient keeps the difference (time constant R0 x Cf2 = seconds).  Check: the same netlist, .op only, with the tolerances of the run and 100x tighter
  (reltol 1e-6, vntol 1e-9); the ADC cell draws the DC load current shown from the amplifier output (driver / TG off-state leakage, about 1 nA at ff 85 C).
  variant        corner      T |     L-U at DC, run tol   L-U at DC, tight tol |      DC load
  orig           typical    27 |        -3.34 uV = -0.004 LSB      -3.34 uV = -0.004 LSB |     0.053 nA
  orig           ff         85 |         3.82 uV = +0.005 LSB       3.82 uV = +0.005 LSB |     1.017 nA
  orig           ss        -40 |        -8.90 uV = -0.011 LSB      -8.90 uV = -0.011 LSB |     0.038 nA
  rvt            typical    27 |         0.07 uV = +0.000 LSB       0.07 uV = +0.000 LSB |    -0.014 nA
  rvt            ff         85 |         0.15 uV = +0.000 LSB       0.15 uV = +0.000 LSB |     0.922 nA
  rvt            ss        -40 |        -0.00 uV = -0.000 LSB      -0.00 uV = -0.000 LSB |    -0.008 nA
  -> the settling result of a variant is CHANGE (and END once STATIC is removed); a STATIC value that vanishes with the tight tolerances is a property of the DC solve, not of the circuit.
